`paginate(items, page, per_page=10)` returns the items on 1-based page number `page` when each page holds `per_page` items. A page before the first or past the end is an empty list.

The implementation below has a bug: it fails at least one of the tests shown. Fix it so every test passes. The fixed function is also run against held-out tests of the same behavior, so fix the bug itself rather than special-casing these tests.

```python
def paginate(items, page, per_page=10):
    if page <= 1:
        return []
    start = (page - 1) * per_page
    return items[start:start + per_page]
```

